  "assertion_excerpts": [
    "lab_linux_test.go:262: Observed: isolated IPv4/IPv6 positive controls, blocked ingress/egress, nft drop counters, extra-interface cleanup refusal, unchanged host network.",
    "safety_linux_test.go:95: Observed: active-process cleanup refused; owned child stayed alive; cleanup succeeded after that child exited.",
    "safety_linux_test.go:157: Observed: exclusive lock blocks competing helpers; shared inspection works; restart retains the same verified namespace without recreation.",
    "safety_linux_test.go:240: Observed: FIFO, symlink, directory, hard link, permissive mode and malformed ownership records were rejected without hanging or touching the peer file.",
    "lab_linux_test.go:176: Observed: cross-UID client created/inspected/cleaned a real quarantine; same-group wrong UID and root rejected; malformed commands and excess idle connections rejected; daemon restart retained and recovered kernel state.",
    "lab_linux_test.go:220: Observed: owned stale socket recovered under lock; live/unowned socket retained and refused.",
    "lab_linux_test.go:296: Observed: client rejected a non-root peer before transmitting a framed request, despite a root-owned socket path.",
    "http_linux_test.go:185: Observed: UID 65534 HTTP control server -> root IPC daemon -> kernel quarantine, CSRF/confirmation required, prepare verified, VPN start still 409, deletion interlock, cleanup and safe deletion.",
    "lab_linux_test.go:425: Observed: mutual TLS handshake with rejected wrong server name; ignored pushed route/DNS; DNS UDP/TCP and business TCP sourced from tunnel; mixed/private DNS rejected; DNS timeout did not fall back; established and new flows blocked after VPN/TUN loss, even with an underlay default route. Counters before=2 after=7; service before={DNSUDP:6 DNSTCP:1 Connections:5 Messages:5 BadSource:0} after={DNSUDP:6 DNSTCP:1 Connections:5 Messages:5 BadSource:0}; host network/DNS unchanged."
